 "result": "**Decorator:** `@needs_app_scope`, defined in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and pushes its app context around your callback.\n\nYou don't need it if you register the command on `app.cli` or `bundle.cli`. Those are `AppGroup`s (`src/tessel/app.py:338`, `src/tessel/bundles.py:49`), whose `.command()` wraps callbacks in `needs_app_scope` automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (line 333) does the loading. `TesselGroup` (line 531), the main `tessel` CLI group, uses it to find the app and list its commands.",
